# Pages whose HAND-WRITTEN text already carries a full date that the family tree attaches to a
# person this archive judges living (tools/gedcom.py classify_living), found on 16 October 2026
# the first time tools/livingcheck.py looked with the GEDCOM beside it. Before that day the only
# date gate (the kit's checkliving.py) read flags in committed data, and the data held none.
#
# THIS FILE NAMES THE PAGE AND HOW MANY. It never records the date or the person: a list of living
# people's dates is exactly what must not be committed. A page listed here may carry up to that
# many; one more fails the build (tools/livingcheck.py, rule GED-DATE).
#
# These are research prose (marriage certificates, corrections, a tree error the archive reports)
# and were NOT rewritten when the living standard was adopted. Each is somebody's decision to make:
# either the person is in fact dead and the tree lacks the death, or the date should come off the
# page. Removing a row here is the goal; adding one needs a reason.
#
# page|count|why
arolsen|1|a date from a transcribed extract, printed with the card
certificate|1|a date from a certificate transcribed in full
sources|1|the same date, quoted in the account of the certificate
people/marica-milkovic|1|a correction quotes a tree entry's birth date to show the tree is wrong
people/domianus-perpic|1|a correction quotes a tree entry's birth date to show the tree is wrong
people/maria-sojath|1|the same correction as on the husband's page
impossible|1|a contradiction listed with the tree entry's own date
corrections|3|the corrections quote the tree entries' dates side by side with the registers
site/src/data/corrections.json|1|the corrections file quotes a tree entry's birth date to show the tree is wrong (hand-kept; it is the text of /corrections/)
site/src/data/sources.json|1|the account of the certificate, quoting the same date (hand-kept; it is the text of /sources/)
site/src/pages/arolsen.astro|1|the page source of /arolsen/: the same date as in the built page
site/src/pages/certificate.astro|1|the page source of /certificate/: the same date as in the built page
